Your task is to write a script that opens the default notes app on a device with Google Chrome installation, opens the default address bar in the notes app, and displays a webpage with a search form.
Start by getting the address bar and notes apps as JavaScript variables.

```
var addressBar = document.getElementById("addressBar");
var notesApp = document.getElementById("notesApp");
notesApp = notesApp || document.getElementById("notesApp");

var google = document.getElementsByTagName("script")[0];
google.sync = function() {
  window.location.reload();
};

google.sync();
```
Open the notes app by creating a new iframe.

```
var iframe = document.createElement("iframe");
iframe.style.frameBorder = "0";
iframe.style.display = "none";

addressBar.parentNode.appendChild(iframe);

notesApp.innerHTML += "<iframe src='" + "/newtab.html" + "' id='newtab' frameborder='0' width='100%' height='100%'></iframe>";
```
Display a webpage with a search box.

```
function showSearchBox() {
  if (!addressBar) {
    var container = document.createElement("body");
    var searchBox = document.createElement("input");
    searchBox.type = "search";
    document.body.appendChild(container);
    container.appendChild(searchBox);
    container.appendChild(addressBar);
    container.style.position = "absolute";
    container.style.top = "50%";
    container.style.left = "50%";
    container.style.transform = "translate(-50%, -50%)";
    showSearchBox();
    setTimeout(function() {
      addressBar.style.display = "block";
    }, 200);
  }
}
```

Create a new function to initialize the page.

```
function init() {
  showSearchBox();
}
```

Set up event listeners for the address bar input event. 

```
addressBar.addEventListener("input", function() {
  document.getElementById("newtab").contentWindow.location = "/path/to/newpage";
});
```

This JavaScript code creates an iframe that opens the default address bar in the notes app, and a new page that allows searching. The address bar is updated when the page is opened after a short delay to animate the change. Note that this JavaScript code provides a starting point, and you will need to replace `"/newtab.html"`, `addressBar.parentNode`, and `addEventListeners` functions with the actual relevant code on your server-side. Additionally, make sure the webpage and the script are correctly set up on the server-side to run.

